import Word
import IO
import Functor
import Sys
import Text
import WordArray

/-!
# Slice 3: the read-only `mmap` page decoder

The read path of the storage engine (`wiz-notes/storage-engine.md`, slice 3): a
read-only mapping of the store's file, the 32-byte page header, the 32-byte primary node
records, the B+tree walk, the two meta slots, and a per-page checksum that can be
skipped on the hot path.

* `Map` is a `foreign_type` in the `lib/Sys.wiz` style: `Map.ofFd` is `mmap` (read-only,
  `PROT_READ | MAP_SHARED`), the finalizer is `munmap`, `Map.len` is the mapped length,
  and `Map.getU64At` is the bounds-checked unaligned wide load (`none` outside the
  mapping) — a bad page number or offset is an error, never a `SIGSEGV`. `Map.getU64`
  is the same load without the check, for offsets a caller has already checked (the
  decoder only uses it after `Store.pageBase` or a meta-slot bound).
* Pages are read in place: a `MappedSnapshot` holds the `Map` handle and a root page number,
  and a lookup copies one 32-byte record, never a page. The mapping is reference
  counted like every other `foreign_type`, so a snapshot kept across a commit keeps its
  mapping alive.
* Writes do not go through the map. The commit path is `pwrite` + `fsync` (slice 2), so
  the mapping is read-only and no `msync` is needed.
* `Store.checkPage`/`MappedSnapshot.getNodeWith`/`MappedSnapshot.indexBucketWith` take a
  `verify : Bool`: `.true` recomputes the page's FNV-1a-64 checksum, `.false` only
  bounds-checks the page. The wrappers `MappedSnapshot.open`, `MappedSnapshot.getNode` and
  `MappedSnapshot.indexBucket` verify by default (the first slice's choice). The meta slots
  are always checksummed (two 64-byte reads per open), so a torn meta write is never
  read.

## The format this decoder assumes (version 2)

`wiz-notes/storage-engine.md` fixes the shape but not every byte value. This decoder was
written before `store-durable` published its writer; the constants below were then pinned
to that writer (the magic, the chained kind-1 leaf, the 96-byte meta record), so the two
halves read and write one format:

* page size 4096 B; page `p` is at `p * 4096`; the file is little-endian;
* page header 32 B: `u16 kind` (0), `u16 n` (2), `u16 free` (4), `u16 flags` (6),
  `u64 txid` (8), `u64 checksum` (16), `u32 right` (24), `u32 reserved` (28);
* page kinds: 1 leaf, 2 internal, 3 index-leaf, 4 index-internal, 5 free, 6 log,
  7 meta (the note lists the kinds but not their numbers). The writer uses kind 1 only:
  the primary records are one chained run of leaves, followed through `right`;
* primary leaf record 32 B: `u64 node id` (0), `u32 kind` (8), `u32 label` (12),
  `u64 count` (16), `u64 version` (24), slots at `32 + i*32` (the note's "the node id
  is the key, so it is not repeated" contradicts its own arithmetic — 32 B a record,
  127 a leaf, the slot at `32 + i*32` — so the explicit field list, which includes the
  key, is the one implemented; a B+tree leaf needs the key to answer a range scan);
* primary internal record 16 B: `u64 key` (0), `u32 child` (8), `u32 pad` (12), slots
  at `32 + i*16`; the child is the last entry whose key is `<=` the target, or the
  first entry when the target is below all of them;
* index leaf record 16 B: `u64 value` (0), `u64 node` (8). The note's "8 B with the
  node id in the value slot" for a unique index has no decodable reading (a lookup by
  value needs the value in the entry), so both kinds use the 16 B record and
  uniqueness stays a constraint, not a layout;
* meta record: the note's field list is 96 B (magic, format, flags, txid, root,
  index_root, freelist_root, log_end, del_epoch, min_gen, schema_gen, page_count,
  checksum) but its text says "two 64-byte slots". The decoder tries 96 B (checksum
  at 88) and then 64 B (checksum at 56), so either choice reads. Fields before
  `index_root` — all the read path needs — are at the same offsets in both;
* meta slots are searched at offsets 0, 64 and 4096, because §2.2 puts slot B on page
  1 and §2.3 puts two 64-byte slots on page 0; the valid slot with the larger `txid`
  wins;
* magic: the note gives no value, so a nonzero magic plus a valid checksum and
  `format = 2` identifies a slot (`Store.metaMagic` is what the writer uses);
* `format = 2`; checksums are FNV-1a-64 over the page (or meta record) with the
  checksum field zeroed, offset basis `0xcbf29ce484222325`, prime `0x100000001b3`;
* never-reuse pages: roots and snapshots are valid forever; compaction renames a new
  file (a mapped snapshot keeps the old inode).
-/

-- ## The mapping: `mmap`/`munmap` and the wide load

/-- A read-only mapping of a store file. Like `Fd`, an ordinary reference-counted
`foreign_type`: copies share the mapping and it is unmapped when the last one goes. -/
foreign_type Map (finalizer := "wiz_store_map_free")
/-- `mmap` the descriptor read-only. `len` is clamped to the file's size (mapping past
the end of a file would `SIGBUS` on the first read there), and 0 is `EINVAL`; an error
is `NULL` and `Sys.errno`. The descriptor may be closed once the map exists. -/
extern "wiz_store_mmap_ro" Map.ofFd : Fd → Nat → IO Map
/-- The mapped length in bytes. -/
extern "wiz_store_map_len" Map.len : Map → Nat
/-- The little-endian `u64` at byte offset `off`, or `none` when the eight bytes are not
all inside the mapping. This is the safe load: an out-of-range offset is a value, not a
fault. Unaligned offsets are fine (`memcpy` in C). -/
extern "wiz_store_get_u64_at" Map.getU64At : Map → Nat → Option U64
/-- The same load without the bounds check. Only for offsets the caller has checked
against `Map.len` (the decoder checks the page once, then reads the page's fields). -/
extern "wiz_store_get_u64" Map.getU64 : Map → Nat → U64

/-- `mmap` a descriptor, failing with the C library's message (`Sys.check`). -/
def Store.mapFile (fd : Fd) (length : Nat) : EIO Map := Sys.check "mmap" (Map.ofFd fd length)

-- ## The format, version 2

/-- `4096`: the unit of COW, checksum and mapping. -/
def Store.pageSize : Nat := 4096
/-- The page header's size in bytes. -/
def Store.headerSize : Nat := 32
/-- A primary node record's size in bytes. -/
def Store.recordSize : Nat := 32
/-- An index leaf record's size in bytes (`value`, `node`). -/
def Store.indexRecordSize : Nat := 16
/-- An internal page record's size (`key`, `child`, `pad`). -/
def Store.internalRecordSize : Nat := 16
/-- The on-disk format version (`meta.format`). Version 2 adds the registry root at meta
offset 40; the read path ignores it, so the fields it uses are unchanged. -/
def Store.formatVersion : Nat := 2
/-- The on-disk magic (`store-durable`'s `metaMagic`). -/
def Store.metaMagic : U64 := U64.ofNat 0x57495a53544f5245
/-- The offsets a meta slot may start at (page 0, its second 64-byte slot, page 1). -/
def Store.metaOffsets : List Nat := [0, 64, 4096]
/-- The deepest tree walk accepted before the file is called cyclic/corrupt. -/
def Store.maxDepth : Nat := 64

/-- The page kinds of version 2. -/
inductive PageKind where
  | leaf
  | internal
  | indexLeaf
  | indexInternal
  | free
  | log
  | meta
  | other (code : Nat)

/-- The kind for a header's `u16`. -/
def PageKind.ofNat (n : Nat) : PageKind :=
  match n with
  | 1 => .leaf
  | 2 => .internal
  | 3 => .indexLeaf
  | 4 => .indexInternal
  | 5 => .free
  | 6 => .log
  | 7 => .meta
  | k => .other k

/-- The number on disk for a kind (`other k` is `k`). -/
def PageKind.code : PageKind → Nat
  | .leaf => 1
  | .internal => 2
  | .indexLeaf => 3
  | .indexInternal => 4
  | .free => 5
  | .log => 6
  | .meta => 7
  | .other k => k

/-- What the decoder refuses. `outOfRange` is a read outside the mapping or a page — the
safe path instead of a fault; `corrupt` is a checksum mismatch. -/
inductive StoreError where
  | outOfRange (what : String) (offset : Nat) (length : Nat)
  | corrupt (page : U64) (expected : U64) (found : U64)
  | badKind (page : U64) (kind : Nat)
  | badMeta
  | badFormat (format : Nat)
  | tooDeep (page : U64)

/-- A readable message (the test prints it; a real caller matches instead). -/
def StoreError.message : StoreError → String
  | .outOfRange what off len =>
    String.append "out of range: " (String.append what
      (String.append " at " (String.append (Nat.toString off)
        (String.append " + " (Nat.toString len)))))
  | .corrupt page expected found =>
    String.append "corrupt page " (String.append (Nat.toString (UIntN.toNat page))
      (String.append ": checksum " (String.append (Nat.toString (UIntN.toNat expected))
        (String.append " != " (Nat.toString (UIntN.toNat found))))))
  | .badKind page kind =>
    String.append "page " (String.append (Nat.toString (UIntN.toNat page))
      (String.append " has kind " (Nat.toString kind)))
  | .badMeta => "no valid meta slot"
  | .badFormat f => String.append "format " (String.append (Nat.toString f) ", expected 2")
  | .tooDeep page =>
    String.append "walk too deep at page " (Nat.toString (UIntN.toNat page))

-- ## The page header

/-- The decoded 32-byte page header. `kindCode` is the `u16` as stored. -/
structure PageHeader where
  kind : PageKind
  kindCode : Nat
  n : Nat
  free : Nat
  flags : Nat
  txid : U64
  checksum : U64
  right : U64

/-- The header at an already-bounds-checked page base. -/
def Store.headerAt (m : Map) (base : Nat) : PageHeader :=
  let w0 := UIntN.toNat (Map.getU64 m base);
  let kind := Nat.land w0 0xffff;
  let right := Nat.land (UIntN.toNat (Map.getU64 m (Nat.add base 24))) 0xffffffff;
  PageHeader.mk (PageKind.ofNat kind) kind
    (Nat.land (Nat.shiftRight w0 16) 0xffff)
    (Nat.land (UIntN.toNat (Map.getU64 m (Nat.add base 4))) 0xffff)
    (Nat.land (Nat.shiftRight (UIntN.toNat (Map.getU64 m (Nat.add base 4))) 16) 0xffff)
    (Map.getU64 m (Nat.add base 8))
    (Map.getU64 m (Nat.add base 16))
    (U64.ofNat right)

/-- The byte offset of page `page`, or `outOfRange` when the whole page is not inside
the mapping. Every tree read starts here; the unchecked `Map.getU64` calls after it are
inside the page. -/
def Store.pageBase (m : Map) (page : U64) : Except StoreError Nat :=
  let off := Nat.mul (UIntN.toNat page) Store.pageSize;
  match Nat.le (Nat.add off Store.pageSize) (Map.len m) with
  | .true => .ok off
  | .false => .error (.outOfRange "page" off Store.pageSize)

/-- The records a leaf page can hold: `(4096 - 32) / 32` = 127. -/
def Store.leafRecCap : Nat := Nat.div (Nat.sub Store.pageSize Store.headerSize) Store.recordSize
/-- The records an internal page (or an index leaf: the same 16-byte slot) can hold: 254. -/
def Store.internalRecCap : Nat :=
  Nat.div (Nat.sub Store.pageSize Store.headerSize) Store.internalRecordSize

/-- A page header's `n`, clamped to the slots that actually fit in the page. `n` is disk
input: `pageBase` bounds the page, but not an index derived from a corrupt count, so
every slot loop caps the header before its unchecked `Map.getU64` calls. A file this
writer produced is unaffected (`n` is the slot count); a corrupt or hostile one reads
garbage slots, never a byte past the mapping. -/
def Store.capSlots (n cap : Nat) : Nat :=
  match Nat.le n cap with
  | .true => n
  | .false => cap

/-- The header of a page, bounds-checked. -/
def Store.header (m : Map) (page : U64) : Except StoreError PageHeader :=
  match Store.pageBase m page with
  | .error e => .error e
  | .ok base => .ok (Store.headerAt m base)

-- ## Checksums: FNV-1a-64, over the page with the checksum field zeroed

/-- FNV-1a-64's offset basis. -/
def Store.fnvOffset : U64 := U64.ofNat 0xcbf29ce484222325
/-- FNV-1a-64's prime. -/
def Store.fnvPrime : U64 := U64.ofNat 0x100000001b3
/-- One FNV-1a-64 byte (the number's low eight bits). -/
def Store.fnvByte (h : U64) (b : Nat) : U64 :=
  UIntN.mul (UIntN.xor h (U64.ofNat (Nat.mod b 256))) Store.fnvPrime

/-- FNV-1a-64 over a byte list (the reference definition; the test builds its fixture
with this one). -/
def Store.fnvBytesFrom : U64 → List Nat → U64
  | h, .nil => h
  | h, .cons b bs => Store.fnvBytesFrom (Store.fnvByte h b) bs

/-- FNV-1a-64 over a byte list. -/
def Store.fnvBytes (bs : List Nat) : U64 := Store.fnvBytesFrom Store.fnvOffset bs

/-- FNV-1a-64 over `bs` with the `skipLen` bytes at `skip` read as zero (the checksum
field): the writer's definition. -/
def Store.fnvExceptFrom : U64 → Nat → Nat → Nat → List Nat → U64
  | h, i, skip, skipLen, .nil => h
  | h, i, skip, skipLen, .cons b bs =>
    let inSkip := if Nat.le skip i then Nat.lt i (Nat.add skip skipLen) else Bool.false;
    Store.fnvExceptFrom (Store.fnvByte h (if inSkip then 0 else b))
      (Nat.succ i) skip skipLen bs

/-- FNV-1a-64 over `bs`, with the checksum field at `skip` zeroed. -/
def Store.fnvExcept (bs : List Nat) (skip : Nat) (skipLen : Nat) : U64 :=
  Store.fnvExceptFrom Store.fnvOffset 0 skip skipLen bs

/-- The checksum of a page image (the field at byte 16 is zeroed). -/
def Store.pageChecksum (bytes : List Nat) : U64 := Store.fnvExcept bytes 16 8

/-- The checksum of a meta record of `width` bytes (the field in its last eight bytes
is zeroed). Only the record's `width` bytes are folded: the rest of the page is not
part of it. -/
def Store.metaChecksumBytes (bytes : List Nat) (width : Nat) : U64 :=
  Store.fnvExcept (List.take width bytes) (Nat.sub width 8) 8

/-- Byte `k` of a little-endian word. -/
def Store.wordByte (w : U64) (k : Nat) : Nat :=
  UIntN.toNat (UIntN.land (UIntN.shiftRight w (Nat.mul 8 k)) (U64.ofNat 255))

/-- One FNV-1a-64 word: its eight little-endian bytes, in order. -/
def Store.fnvWord (h0 : U64) (w : U64) : U64 :=
  let h1 := Store.fnvByte h0 (Store.wordByte w 0);
  let h2 := Store.fnvByte h1 (Store.wordByte w 1);
  let h3 := Store.fnvByte h2 (Store.wordByte w 2);
  let h4 := Store.fnvByte h3 (Store.wordByte w 3);
  let h5 := Store.fnvByte h4 (Store.wordByte w 4);
  let h6 := Store.fnvByte h5 (Store.wordByte w 5);
  let h7 := Store.fnvByte h6 (Store.wordByte w 6);
  Store.fnvByte h7 (Store.wordByte w 7)

/-- The page's checksum, folded eight bytes at a time. `i` is the word index, `fuel` the
words left; word 2 (byte 16, the checksum field) reads as zero. -/
def Store.pageChecksumFrom : Map → Nat → Nat → Nat → U64 → U64
  | m, base, i, .zero, h => h
  | m, base, i, .succ f, h =>
    let w := match Nat.beq i 2 with
      | .true => U64.ofNat 0
      | .false => Map.getU64 m (Nat.add base (Nat.mul i 8));
    Store.pageChecksumFrom m base (Nat.succ i) f (Store.fnvWord h w)

/-- The checksum stored in the header of a page (bounds-checked). -/
def Store.pageChecksumAt (m : Map) (page : U64) : Except StoreError U64 :=
  match Store.pageBase m page with
  | .error e => .error e
  | .ok base => .ok (Store.pageChecksumFrom m base 0 (Nat.div Store.pageSize 8) Store.fnvOffset)

/-- Verify a page's checksum. -/
def Store.verifyPage (m : Map) (page : U64) : Except StoreError Unit :=
  match Store.pageBase m page with
  | .error e => .error e
  | .ok base =>
    let hdr := Store.headerAt m base;
    let found := Store.pageChecksumFrom m base 0 (Nat.div Store.pageSize 8) Store.fnvOffset;
    match UIntN.beq hdr.checksum found with
    | .true => .ok ()
    | .false => .error (.corrupt page hdr.checksum found)

/-- Bounds-check a page, and verify its checksum when `verify` (the option the hot path
turns off; the callers below default it on). -/
def Store.checkPage (m : Map) (page : U64) (verify : Bool) : Except StoreError Unit :=
  match verify with
  | .true => Store.verifyPage m page
  | .false => match Store.pageBase m page with
    | .error e => .error e
    | .ok _ => .ok ()

-- ## Primary node records

/-- The 32-byte record: the key (the node id) is stored first, then the fields. -/
structure NodeRecord where
  id : U64
  kind : U64
  label : U64
  count : U64
  version : U64

/-- The record at slot `i` of an already-checked leaf page. -/
def Store.recordAt (m : Map) (base : Nat) (i : Nat) : NodeRecord :=
  let off := Nat.add base (Nat.add Store.headerSize (Nat.mul i Store.recordSize));
  let kindLabel := Map.getU64 m (Nat.add off 8);
  NodeRecord.mk (Map.getU64 m off)
    (UIntN.resize 64 (UIntN.land kindLabel (U64.ofNat 0xffffffff)))
    (UIntN.resize 64 (UIntN.shiftRight kindLabel 32))
    (Map.getU64 m (Nat.add off 16))
    (Map.getU64 m (Nat.add off 24))

/-- Record `i` of a leaf page, checking the kind and the slot. -/
def Store.nodeInLeaf (m : Map) (page : U64) (i : Nat) : Except StoreError NodeRecord :=
  match Store.header m page with
  | .error e => .error e
  | .ok hdr =>
    match hdr.kind with
    | .leaf =>
      match Nat.lt i (Store.capSlots hdr.n Store.leafRecCap) with
      | .true => match Store.pageBase m page with
        | .error e => .error e
        | .ok base => .ok (Store.recordAt m base i)
      | .false => .error (.outOfRange "leaf entry" i hdr.n)
    | _ => .error (.badKind page hdr.kindCode)

/-- Scan a leaf from slot `i`, `fuel` slots left, for `key`. -/
def Store.findInLeafFrom : Map → Nat → Nat → Nat → U64 → Option NodeRecord
  | m, base, i, .zero, key => .none
  | m, base, i, .succ f, key =>
    let rec := Store.recordAt m base i;
    match UIntN.beq rec.id key with
    | .true => .some rec
    | .false => Store.findInLeafFrom m base (Nat.succ i) f key

/-- The node with `key` in a leaf page (linear in `n`, at most 127 slots). -/
def Store.findInLeaf (m : Map) (page : U64) (key : U64) : Except StoreError (Option NodeRecord) :=
  match Store.header m page with
  | .error e => .error e
  | .ok hdr =>
    match hdr.kind with
    | .leaf => match Store.pageBase m page with
      | .error e => .error e
      | .ok base => .ok (Store.findInLeafFrom m base 0
          (Store.capSlots hdr.n Store.leafRecCap) key)
    | _ => .error (.badKind page hdr.kindCode)

/-- Scan a leaf, then its `right` siblings: `store-durable` writes the primary records as
one chained run of leaf pages (no internal pages yet), so a lookup that is not in the
first page follows the chain. `fuel` bounds a corrupt cycle. -/
def Store.findInChain : Map → U64 → U64 → Bool → Nat → Except StoreError (Option NodeRecord)
  | _, _, _, _, .zero => .error (.tooDeep 0)
  | m, page, key, verify, .succ f => match Store.checkPage m page verify with
    | .error e => .error e
    | .ok _ => match Store.header m page with
      | .error e => .error e
      | .ok hdr => match hdr.kind with
        | .leaf => match Store.findInLeaf m page key with
          | .error e => .error e
          | .ok (.some r) => .ok (.some r)
          | .ok .none => match UIntN.beq hdr.right (U64.ofNat 0) with
            | .true => .ok .none
            | .false => Store.findInChain m hdr.right key verify f
        | _ => .error (.badKind page hdr.kindCode)

-- ## The B+tree walk

/-- The child for `key`: the last internal entry whose key is `<= key`, or the first
entry when every key is greater (which the leaf search then answers with `none`). -/
def Store.childFrom : Map → Nat → Nat → Nat → U64 → Option U64 → Option U64
  | m, base, i, .zero, key, best => best
  | m, base, i, .succ f, key, best =>
    let ekey := Map.getU64 m (Nat.add base (Nat.add Store.headerSize (Nat.mul i Store.internalRecordSize)));
    let echild := UIntN.resize 64 (UIntN.land
      (Map.getU64 m (Nat.add base (Nat.add 40 (Nat.mul i Store.internalRecordSize))))
      (U64.ofNat 0xffffffff));
    let best' := match UIntN.le ekey key with
      | .true => .some echild
      | .false => best;
    Store.childFrom m base (Nat.succ i) f key best'

/-- The child of an internal page with `n` entries (primary or index: same shape). `n` is
capped to the 254 slots that fit before any unchecked load. -/
def Store.findChildOf (m : Map) (page : U64) (n : Nat) (key : U64) : Except StoreError U64 :=
  let n := Store.capSlots n Store.internalRecCap;
  match n with
  | 0 => .error (.outOfRange "internal entry" 0 0)
  | _ => match Store.pageBase m page with
    | .error e => .error e
    | .ok base =>
      let first := UIntN.resize 64 (UIntN.land
        (Map.getU64 m (Nat.add base 40)) (U64.ofNat 0xffffffff));
      .ok (match Store.childFrom m base 0 n key .none with
        | .some c => c
        | .none => first)

/-- The child page of an internal page for `key`. -/
def Store.findChild (m : Map) (page : U64) (key : U64) : Except StoreError U64 :=
  match Store.header m page with
  | .error e => .error e
  | .ok hdr =>
    match hdr.kind with
    | .internal => Store.findChildOf m page hdr.n key
    | .indexInternal => Store.findChildOf m page hdr.n key
    | _ => .error (.badKind page hdr.kindCode)

/-- Walk from `page` to the node with `key`, `fuel` pages deep. Every page is checked
(and, with `verify`, checksummed) on the way down. -/
def Store.walkFrom : Map → U64 → U64 → Bool → Nat → Except StoreError (Option NodeRecord)
  | m, page, key, verify, .zero => .error (.tooDeep page)
  | m, page, key, verify, .succ f => match Store.checkPage m page verify with
    | .error e => .error e
    | .ok _ => match Store.header m page with
      | .error e => .error e
      | .ok hdr => match hdr.kind with
        | .leaf => Store.findInChain m page key verify f
        | .internal => match Store.findChild m page key with
          | .error e => .error e
          | .ok child => Store.walkFrom m child key verify f
        | _ => .error (.badKind page hdr.kindCode)

/-- The node with `key` under `root`: the snapshot root → pages path, verifying every
page (the option is `walkFrom`'s). -/
def Store.getNode (m : Map) (root : U64) (key : U64) (verify : Bool) :
    Except StoreError (Option NodeRecord) :=
  Store.walkFrom m root key verify Store.maxDepth

-- ## Index leaves

/-- The `value` of index slot `i` of an already-checked leaf. -/
def Store.indexValueAt (m : Map) (base : Nat) (i : Nat) : U64 :=
  Map.getU64 m (Nat.add base (Nat.add Store.headerSize (Nat.mul i Store.indexRecordSize)))

/-- The `node` of index slot `i` of an already-checked leaf. -/
def Store.indexNodeAt (m : Map) (base : Nat) (i : Nat) : U64 :=
  Map.getU64 m (Nat.add base (Nat.add 40 (Nat.mul i Store.indexRecordSize)))

/-- Collect the nodes whose value is `target` from slot `i`, `fuel` slots left, into
`acc` (reversed). -/
def Store.collectBucketFrom : Map → Nat → Nat → Nat → U64 → List U64 → List U64
  | m, base, i, .zero, target, acc => acc
  | m, base, i, .succ f, target, acc =>
    let v := Store.indexValueAt m base i;
    let acc' := match UIntN.beq v target with
      | .true => List.cons (Store.indexNodeAt m base i) acc
      | .false => acc;
    Store.collectBucketFrom m base (Nat.succ i) f target acc'

/-- An index leaf's bucket, following the `right` sibling links while they last. -/
def Store.collectLeafChain : Map → U64 → U64 → Bool → Nat → Except StoreError (List U64)
  | m, page, target, verify, .zero => .error (.tooDeep page)
  | m, page, target, verify, .succ f => match Store.checkPage m page verify with
    | .error e => .error e
    | .ok _ => match Store.header m page with
      | .error e => .error e
      | .ok hdr => match hdr.kind with
        | .indexLeaf => match Store.pageBase m page with
          | .error e => .error e
          | .ok base =>
            let here := List.reverse
              (Store.collectBucketFrom m base 0
                (Store.capSlots hdr.n Store.internalRecCap) target []);
            match UIntN.beq hdr.right (U64.ofNat 0) with
            | .true => .ok here
            | .false => match Store.collectLeafChain m hdr.right target verify f with
              | .error e => .error e
              | .ok rest => .ok (List.append here rest)
        | _ => .error (.badKind page hdr.kindCode)

/-- The nodes in the index bucket for `value`, from an index root. Index internal pages
have the primary internal shape. -/
def Store.indexWalk : Map → U64 → U64 → Bool → Nat → Except StoreError (List U64)
  | m, page, target, verify, .zero => .error (.tooDeep page)
  | m, page, target, verify, .succ f => match Store.checkPage m page verify with
    | .error e => .error e
    | .ok _ => match Store.header m page with
      | .error e => .error e
      | .ok hdr => match hdr.kind with
        | .indexLeaf => Store.collectLeafChain m page target verify f
        | .indexInternal => match Store.findChild m page target with
          | .error e => .error e
          | .ok child => Store.indexWalk m child target verify f
        | _ => .error (.badKind page hdr.kindCode)

-- ## The meta slots

/-- The fields of one meta slot that the read path uses; `width` is the record size the
checksum matched (64 or 96). -/
structure MetaSlot where
  offset : Nat
  width : Nat
  format : Nat
  txid : U64
  root : U64
  indexRoot : U64
  pageCount : U64
  delEpoch : U64

/-- FNV-1a-64 over a meta record (`width` bytes), the last word zeroed. -/
def Store.metaChecksumFrom : Map → Nat → Nat → Nat → Nat → U64 → U64
  | m, off, i, .zero, last, h => h
  | m, off, i, .succ f, last, h =>
    let w := match Nat.beq i last with
      | .true => U64.ofNat 0
      | .false => Map.getU64 m (Nat.add off (Nat.mul i 8));
    Store.metaChecksumFrom m off (Nat.succ i) f last (Store.fnvWord h w)

/-- The checksum a `width`-byte meta record should have. -/
def Store.metaChecksum (m : Map) (off : Nat) (width : Nat) : U64 :=
  let words := Nat.div width 8;
  Store.metaChecksumFrom m off 0 words (Nat.sub words 1) Store.fnvOffset

/-- The record's checksum field. -/
def Store.metaStoredChecksum (m : Map) (off : Nat) (width : Nat) : U64 :=
  Map.getU64 m (Nat.add off (Nat.sub width 8))

/-- The record's fields (the caller has bounds-checked `width` bytes). -/
def Store.metaRecord (m : Map) (off : Nat) (width : Nat) : MetaSlot :=
  let w1 := UIntN.toNat (Map.getU64 m (Nat.add off 8));
  MetaSlot.mk off width (Nat.land w1 0xffffffff)
    (Map.getU64 m (Nat.add off 16))
    (Map.getU64 m (Nat.add off 24))
    (Map.getU64 m (Nat.add off 32))
    (match Nat.beq width 64 with
      | .true => U64.ofNat 0
      | .false => Map.getU64 m (Nat.add off 80))
    (match Nat.beq width 64 with
      | .true => U64.ofNat 0
      | .false => Map.getU64 m (Nat.add off 56))

/-- The slot at `off`: a nonzero magic and a checksum that matches 96 bytes (the full
field list) or 64 (the short layout). -/
def Store.metaSlotAt (m : Map) (off : Nat) : Except StoreError MetaSlot :=
  match Nat.le (Nat.add off 64) (Map.len m) with
  | .false => .error (.outOfRange "meta slot" off 64)
  | .true =>
    match UIntN.beq (Map.getU64 m off) (U64.ofNat 0) with
    | .true => .error .badMeta
    | .false =>
      let ok96 := match Nat.le (Nat.add off 96) (Map.len m) with
        | .true => UIntN.beq (Store.metaStoredChecksum m off 96)
            (Store.metaChecksum m off 96)
        | .false => Bool.false;
      match ok96 with
      | .true => .ok (Store.metaRecord m off 96)
      | .false =>
        let ok64 := UIntN.beq (Store.metaStoredChecksum m off 64)
          (Store.metaChecksum m off 64);
        match ok64 with
        | .true => .ok (Store.metaRecord m off 64)
        | .false => .error .badMeta

/-- The valid slot with the larger `txid` among `offsets`, or `none`. -/
def Store.pickMetaFrom : Map → Option MetaSlot → List Nat → Option MetaSlot
  | m, best, .nil => best
  | m, best, .cons off offs =>
    let best' := match Store.metaSlotAt m off with
      | .error _ => best
      | .ok s => match best with
        | .none => .some s
        | .some b => match UIntN.lt b.txid s.txid with
          | .true => .some s
          | .false => best;
    Store.pickMetaFrom m best' offs

/-- The meta slot the read path uses: the valid slot with the larger `txid`. Both slots
are always checksummed (two small reads), so a torn write is never read. -/
def Store.pickMeta (m : Map) : Except StoreError MetaSlot :=
  match Store.pickMetaFrom m .none Store.metaOffsets with
  | .some s => .ok s
  | .none => .error .badMeta

-- ## A snapshot is a root pointer

/-- A mapping and a root page: the mapped root (the prototype's is a `U64Map`).
The map is a reference-counted handle; copying the root does not copy a page. -/
structure MapRoot where
  map : Map
  page : U64

/-- An immutable snapshot: a generation and a root page into the mapping. `getDb`
returns one; reads go through `MappedSnapshot.getNode`/`MappedSnapshot.indexBucket`. -/
structure MappedSnapshot where
  gen : U64
  root : MapRoot
  indexRoot : U64

/-- Open a snapshot: pick the valid meta slot, require format 1, and (with `verify`)
checksum the root page. The meta checksums are always checked. -/
def MappedSnapshot.openWith (m : Map) (verify : Bool) : Except StoreError MappedSnapshot :=
  match Store.pickMeta m with
  | .error e => .error e
  | .ok meta => match Nat.beq meta.format Store.formatVersion with
    | .false => .error (.badFormat meta.format)
    | .true => match verify with
      | .false => .ok (MappedSnapshot.mk meta.txid (MapRoot.mk m meta.root) meta.indexRoot)
      | .true => match Nat.beq meta.root.toNat 0 with
        | .true => .ok (MappedSnapshot.mk meta.txid (MapRoot.mk m meta.root) meta.indexRoot)
        | .false => match Store.verifyPage m meta.root with
          | .error e => .error e
          | .ok _ => .ok (MappedSnapshot.mk meta.txid (MapRoot.mk m meta.root) meta.indexRoot)

/-- Open a snapshot, verifying the root page's checksum (the default). -/
def MappedSnapshot.open (m : Map) : Except StoreError MappedSnapshot := MappedSnapshot.openWith m .true

/-- The node with `id` in the snapshot, verifying every page on the way (the first
slice's default). -/
def MappedSnapshot.getNode (s : MappedSnapshot) (id : U64) : Except StoreError (Option NodeRecord) :=
  Store.getNode s.root.map s.root.page id .true

/-- The node with `id`, skipping page checksums on the hot path (`verify := false` only
for pages the caller trusts). -/
def MappedSnapshot.getNodeWith (s : MappedSnapshot) (id : U64) (verify : Bool) :
    Except StoreError (Option NodeRecord) :=
  Store.getNode s.root.map s.root.page id verify

/-- The nodes in the index bucket for `value`, verifying every page (the default). -/
def MappedSnapshot.indexBucket (s : MappedSnapshot) (value : U64) : Except StoreError (List U64) :=
  Store.indexWalk s.root.map s.indexRoot value .true Store.maxDepth

/-- The index bucket, skipping page checksums on the hot path. -/
def MappedSnapshot.indexBucketWith (s : MappedSnapshot) (value : U64) (verify : Bool) :
    Except StoreError (List U64) :=
  Store.indexWalk s.root.map s.indexRoot value verify Store.maxDepth

/-- Map a file and open a snapshot from it: the IO shell the engine's `getDb` uses
(`mapFile` then `MappedSnapshot.openWith`). -/
def Store.openSnapshot (fd : Fd) (length : Nat) (verify : Bool) :
    EIO (Except StoreError MappedSnapshot) := do
  m ← Store.mapFile fd length;
  EIO.pure (MappedSnapshot.openWith m verify)
